      "seconds": 1.058,
      "text": "Reserved synthetic language, seed 104729. Three word meanings are supplied. No model receives the answer key."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 15.148,
      "text": "These known stems are the starting information budget. The plural rule is still uncertain."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 29.487,
      "text": "Two supplied hypotheses disagree: does the plural marker precede or follow the stem? This is candidate testing, not unrestricted discovery."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 43.758,
      "text": "The selector records a discriminating question and its predicted answer groups. Only the stars can be observed in this run."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 57.827,
      "text": "One answer is revealed by the independent corpus oracle. The learner never receives the other answers or hidden rule choice."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 72.073,
      "text": "The observation is retained, and two alternatives become one. The answer does not silently modify executable rules."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 87.091,
      "text": "A deliberate review disables the contradicted rule. Its notebook text and the original elicitation history remain available."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 101.189,
      "text": "Now test the rocks: a plural form that was withheld from the question and observation. Lexical lookup alone cannot resolve it."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 115.296,
      "text": "Symbolic parsing produces the rocks, with a meaning tree, source spans and the exact plural rule used. No language model generated this result."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 129.399,
      "text": "Inspect the derivation: the stem provides the noun meaning, and the retained plural rule composes the unseen form."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 144.131,
      "text": "Reloading restores the saved project and translation draft. Re-running the parser gives the same result."
    },
    {
      "seconds": 158.256,
      "text": "The retained question, answer and review explain the outcome. This narrow regular-plural success does not establish general language-decipherment accuracy."
